{"toolCallId":"call_fb56033c6dfb4f12aa29cb8c778cf725","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"FILE_EXISTS\tauthored_template\terror\tValidates required spec documents for the declared documentation level.\nPLACEHOLDER_FILLED\tauthored_template\terror\tRejects unfilled template placeholders in authored spec documents.\nCOMMENT_HYGIENE_MARKER\tauthored_template\terror\tRejects ephemeral finding markers inside HTML comments in authored spec documents.\nSCAFFOLD_NEVER_TOUCHED\tauthored_template\terror\tRejects scaffold-signature markers in required docs when spec.md claims Complete status.\nSTATUS_CROSS_DOC_CONSISTENCY\tauthored_template\terror\tAdvisory-by-default check that spec.md and implementation-summary.md status fields classify to the same delivery state.\nLEVEL_DECLARED\tauthored_template\tinfo\tReports whether the documentation level was declared or inferred.\nAC_COVERAGE\tauthored_template\tinfo\tDefault-on advisory (non-blocking) scan for acceptance-criteria traceability coverage; set SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE=false to opt out.\nAC_CLOSURE\tauthored_template\terror\tGates packet closure on acceptance-criteria.md at Levels 2, 3 and 3+; unmet criteria block a completion claim and a waiver must cite an ADR that exists. Packets created before the cutoff stay advisory.\nANCHORS_VALID\tauthored_template\terror\tChecks anchors in each spec doc whose template defines them, ignoring fenced code; a phase parent is exempt, and research/research.md and review/review-report.md are skipped as free-form workflow documents. Errors: a doc with no anchors, an anchor opened twice, never closed, closed but never opened, or closed more times than it is opened. Nesting is also an error: an anchor opened inside another, closed before it is opened, or closed while another is still open, though markers quoted in inline code are ignored by the nesting check; an adr-NNN anchor may hold adr-NNN-* anchors. Template order is not checked.\nFRONTMATTER_MEMORY_BLOCK\tauthored_template\terror\tValidates canonical _memory continuity frontmatter blocks.\nMERGE_LEGALITY\toperational_runtime\terror\tValidates generated merge payloads against target anchor shape.\nSPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY\tauthored_template\terror\tChecks implementation-summary sufficiency after save/write flows.\nCROSS_ANCHOR_CONTAMINATION\toperational_runtime\terror\tDetects route/category mismatches before generated content is merged.\nPOST_SAVE_FINGERPRINT\toperational_runtime\terror\tVerifies post-save fingerprints for generated writes.\nTOC_POLICY\tauthored_template\terror\tEnforces table-of-contents placement policy.\nAI_PROTOCOLS\tauthored_template\terror\tValidates AI execution protocol sections in high-governance specs.\nCOMPLEXITY_MATCH\tauthored_template\terror\tChecks declared level against content complexity signals.\nFOLDER_NAMING\tauthored_template\terror\tValidates numbered spec-folder naming conventions.\nFRONTMATTER_VALID\tauthored_template\terror\tValidates YAML frontmatter structure and required semantic values.\nFRONTMATTER_VALUES\tauthored_template\twarn\tWarns when a packet document's contextType or importance_tier is outside the shared list in sk-doc/sk-create-frontmatter/assets/frontmatter-values.json. Aliases are legal.\nSOURCE_TAGS\tauthored_template\twarn\tWarns when a path:line citation inside a [SOURCE: ...] tag in a packet's research or review artifacts names a gone file, a moved file or a line past the end, using sk-doc's citation resolver. Packets created on or before the cutoff are skipped. A pass means the path and line exist, not that they support the claim.\nGREP_CONVENTION\tauthored_template\terror\tChecks every markdown document in a spec folder against the greppable-corpus convention: frontmatter variant, trigger phrase quality, anchor grammar and naming.\nLEVEL_MATCH\tauthored_template\terror\tChecks required files match the declared documentation level.\nGRAPH_METADATA_PRESENT\toperational_runtime\twarn\tChecks generated description and graph metadata are present.\nGRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_DRIFT\toperational_runtime\twarn\tFlags graph-metadata.json children_ids missing on-disk phase children the writer would add (advisory unless SPECKIT_CHILD_DRIFT_ENFORCE=true).\nGRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_IDENTITY\tstructural\terror\tFlags graph-metadata.json children_ids entries whose leading path identity is not the packet's own current identity (stale rename residue the refresh writer now prunes).\nGRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE\tstructural\twarn\tValidates graph-metadata.json shape: required packet/derived blocks, last_active_child_id pointer integrity for phase parents.\nMETADATA_DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY\tstructural\terror\tAdvisory-by-default check that description.json, graph-metadata.json, and continuity ids match the real on-disk spec-folder path.\nDESCRIPTION_SHAPE\tstructural\twarn\tValidates description.json shape: required name/description/level keys present and well-typed.\nNORMALIZER_LINT\toperational_runtime\terror\tStrict-only lint for duplicated runtime normalizer helpers.\nSPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY\tauthored_template\terror\tVerifies inline markdown references resolve within spec docs.\nTEMPLATE_SOURCE\tauthored_template\terror\tChecks SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE provenance markers.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_ROOT_SPEC_REQUIRED\toperational_runtime\terror\tEnsures canonical saves include a root spec reference.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_SOURCE_DOCS_REQUIRED\toperational_runtime\terror\tEnsures canonical saves include source document references.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_LINEAGE_REQUIRED\toperational_runtime\terror\tEnsures canonical save lineage metadata is present.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_PACKET_IDENTITY_NORMALIZED\toperational_runtime\terror\tChecks canonical save packet identity normalization.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_DESCRIPTION_GRAPH_FRESHNESS\toperational_runtime\terror\tChecks generated description/graph freshness for canonical saves.\nCONTINUITY_FRESHNESS\toperational_runtime\terror\tSTRICT\tStrict-mode freshness check for continuity frontmatter. The rule reports warn by default and escalates to fail under SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS_ENFORCE; the ceiling here has to allow that escalation, since a warn ceiling would silently cap it.\nGENERATED_METADATA_INTEGRITY\tstructural\terror\tSTRICT\tValidates description.json and graph-metadata.json through the shared schemas plus path-prefix and status-enum invariants, error under strict behind a grandfather report mode.\nGENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT\tstructural\terror\tSTRICT\tRe-derives a folder and reports drift between the stored description/causal_summary and the current docs, read-only, error under strict only when the drift-gate flag is on and otherwise grandfather report mode.\nLINKS_VALID\toperational_runtime\twarn\tScans the system-spec-kit skill's own markdown for wikilinks whose target file does not exist. The target is always this skill, never the validated packet.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/222-deepseek-baseline","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"9f0b12","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
